## Rulings on the findings (numbers are the review's)
1. Version binding. The program version becomes a field that travels with the model: written at training bind time into the checkpoint and the export, read by every session builder (scripts/acceptance_live_adapter.py and every other place a LiveSession is built). No default: a session builder that finds no version refuses with a typed error, except for exports made before this field existed, which need an explicit `trace_program_version` in the run config. A 3.13 session refuses every 3.14-only form (`rule="box_grid_5cm"`, `<gap camera=...>`, multi-instance entries) with a typed error instead of returning a number, and a 3.14 session refuses 3.13-only forms the same way. Tests: both refusals; a 3.14 export loaded with no config runs 3.14; a mismatched config refuses.
2. Missing boxes and fragments. Follow prog_v2: an instance without a box, or whose largest-mask frame did not lift, is skipped and the category continues with the rest; the category is `box unavailable` only when no instance remains. Add a mask pixel floor as one named key (`min_mask_px`) used identically by the generator and the runtime and recorded in the manifest; default it to the floor prog_v2 or gt_ceiling's pricing used for a valid instance (state which value and where you found it; if none exists, use 39 px, the ground-truth instance floor in grd_selector's set metrics, and say so). Tests with fragment masks: counts are not inflated, and a name is not pushed to `unresolved` by fragments.
3. Exact-frame gate. Make the gate key on a field that production objects carry (find what identifies a frame on the production sighting or instance class; do not add a test-only attribute), and prove it with the production class: an odd frame under paired depth must use its own depth or refuse with a typed error, never a neighbour's depth.
4. Camera-gap instance. prog_v2 (the measured reference) takes the largest-mask instance; the runtime and the generator take the nearest. Price both rules on ground-truth inputs with gt_ceiling's replay harness on every camera-to-object item available locally (state n and the paired difference), adopt the better one, and if the difference is inside its interval adopt prog_v2's rule. Make the generator and the runtime identical on it, and make the generator emit `<gap camera=...>` rows: the review found no training row with that form, so the form would be untrained.
5. Tests that run the risky paths. (a) The production round trip must cover every program type the leg trains (add counting, size, camera and room rows; report the count per type; zero for any type is a failure). (b) Add a perception-path round trip: instead of feeding the generator's own boxes back, feed masks and depth with realistic defects (a missing instance, a fragment, an empty mask, a frame gap, an unknown category, a NaN depth cell) and assert, per defect, either the same answer as prog_v2 on the same inputs or a typed refusal that the caller turns into the direct-answer fallback; never a plausible wrong number. (c) Run the verifier and the tokenization unmocked at least once with the real tokenizer files the tree's tests already use.
7. Dead renderers. `render()` and `render_camera` in this tree raise under 3.14 with a message naming the real generator, or are removed from the import surface.
Finding 6 (point cap 20,000 against 4,000) needs no change; record it.

